{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>עוברי בעמק הבכא</b> — the name of a place, or a valley where there are trees called בכאים." "<b>וטעם מעיין ישיתוהו</b> — because of the many pilgrims in the valley, rain would fall there, and because of the feet of those passing through, the waters were always found there, as though a spring were set there. And note that it is deficient [in spelling], like מעיין ישיתוהו, like אש אוכלה הוא." "<b>גם ברכות יעטה מורה</b> — the road, because of the abundance of water. This is like 'your breakers and your waves' (משבריך וגליך), as I have explained. Rabbi Judah said: מורה is the name of a place, like 'the hill of Moreh' (מגבעת המורה). 'In the valley' is a verse in Samuel."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :notes {1 "The comment refers to a kethiv/qere-type deficiency in the spelling of מעין; the exact letter deficiency is not specified by Ibn Ezra and has been left untranslated as written.", 2 "The phrase 'בעמק פסוק הוא בשמואל' is rendered hyper-literally; it apparently cross-references 1 Samuel 17:2 but the syntax is compressed and somewhat obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:02.498485431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}